# About the Lab Environment

The demonstrations throughout this handbook were performed in a Microsoft Azure environment using Microsoft Sentinel connected to an Azure Log Analytics Workspace. Authentication logs were ingested into a custom table and analyzed using Kusto Query Language (KQL) to simulate a Security Operations Center workflow.

Where appropriate, notes are included to distinguish between educational lab configurations and practices that would typically be used in a production enterprise deployment.

---

# Conclusion

Security Operations Centers are more than dashboards and alerts. Effective security monitoring requires understanding how telemetry is collected, how detections are engineered, how investigations are performed, and how incidents are managed.

The following chapters progressively build this knowledge, beginning with the fundamentals of Security Operations Centers and Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) platforms before moving into Microsoft Sentinel-specific implementation details.
